		{"id":"uncertainty","type":"text","x":0,"y":1870,"width":500,"height":330,"color":"2","text":"### Uncertainty<br><br>- Child findings may not transfer to adults<br>- Support outcomes reflect who chose them<br>- Risk genes do not determine traits"},
		{"id":"hypothesis","type":"text","x":560,"y":1870,"width":560,"height":330,"color":"6","text":"### Open questions<br><br>- Which outcomes do autistic people themselves prioritise, and how are they measured?<br>- How do rare and common variation combine in individual developmental trajectories?<br>- Which adult service models have measured effects, in which systems, and on which outcomes?"},
